  "ingredients": [
    "0.25 cup soy sauce",
    "2 tablespoons honey",
    "4 teaspoons sesame oil",
    "2 cloves garlic, crushed",
    "3 slices fresh ginger root",
    "4 skinless, boneless chicken breast halves"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/op3JPGyQq5WOa08FSLv1ZULvEIQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-8919-Grilled-Asian-Chicken-DDMFS-Step-01a-30eaf72277084732820dbd7c60f6afc5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8919/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine soy sauce, honey, sesame oil, garlic, and ginger in a small microwave-safe bowl; heat in the microwave on medium power for 1 minute, then stir. Heat again for 30 seconds, watching closely to prevent boiling.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Jj-rc90QZEGZ6FKxRsUDVGSYz8E=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-8919-Grilled-Asian-Chicken-DDMFS-Step-1b-d5f7f041c5b24284bcc055e21585bf31.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8919/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chicken breasts in a shallow dish. Pour soy sauce mixture over top and set aside to marinate for 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/178Fi8kI5ijDmixERqMmbPU7I_0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-8919-Grilled-Asian-Chicken-DDMFS-Step-02-40e124fb7bae48fea5a6af63821a4485.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8919/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate. Meanwhile, remove chicken from marinade; transfer marinade into a small saucepan and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low and simmer until thick, about 1 minute. Set aside for basting.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/e6MuId9KXbBeXSzqSrGhIVrWgxQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-8919-Grilled-Asian-Chicken-DDMFS-Step-03-25ed6942a11747ca9298888251cd4155.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8919/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook chicken on the preheated grill, basting frequently with reserved marinade, until golden brown on all sides and chicken is no longer pink in the center, about 6 to 8 minutes per side. An instant-read meat thermometer inserted into the thickest piece should read at least 160 degrees F (70 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/8lrujWA_uSA6naOD-ntDcsoLD3c=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-8919-Grilled-Asian-Chicken-DDMFS-Step-05-2ee614d5331347c99ad77c20893b2470.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8919/step_05.webp"
    }
  ],
